741
00:45:37,735 --> 00:45:41,068
Well, little Billy Barty's here.

742
00:45:41,905 --> 00:45:46,899
-You're not feeling too good, Billy?
-Miss Dawson, my tummy hurts.

743
00:45:47,211 --> 00:45:49,679
Why don't you just lay back and relax?

744
00:45:50,314 --> 00:45:51,804
That was nice. Good job.

745
00:45:51,982 --> 00:45:55,713
I've got too much doo-doo in my underpants.

746
00:45:56,820 --> 00:45:59,118
Make the stinky go away.

747
00:45:59,523 --> 00:46:02,356
Well, you sound like
you got your hands full, so...

748
00:46:02,559 --> 00:46:04,322
...I'll just come out with it.

749
00:46:04,828 --> 00:46:07,319
How would you like
to do something with me tonight?

750
00:46:08,198 --> 00:46:09,961
I'd love to do something with you.

751
00:46:10,200 --> 00:46:11,098
Great.

752
00:46:11,301 --> 00:46:13,963
We can't go out drinking.
I got our company in trouble.

753
00:46:14,037 --> 00:46:17,666
That's okay.
I was brought up never to drink alcohol.

754
00:46:18,375 --> 00:46:20,343
Not even rum raisin ice cream.

755
00:46:20,611 --> 00:46:22,943
I like that. I'll think of something good.

756
00:46:23,814 --> 00:46:24,644
See you tonight.

757
00:46:24,915 --> 00:46:25,904
Okay. 'Bye.

758
00:46:30,053 --> 00:46:31,577
I got to try this.

759
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:45,799
Was that awesome?

760
00:46:47,538 --> 00:46:49,165
Am I out or safe?

761
00:46:51,008 --> 00:46:52,475
I'm with you.

762
00:46:54,411 --> 00:46:58,074
What is this? My great-uncle's personal journal.

763
00:46:59,616 --> 00:47:02,084
-Should I read it?
-Family.

764
00:47:03,821 --> 00:47:05,618
Family, safe, good.

765
00:47:06,023 --> 00:47:09,686
All right, have a good night. My back hurts!

766
00:47:14,531 --> 00:47:16,931
-Nice doing business with you.
-Thank you.

767
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:18,558
Thanks for the bikes.

768
00:47:18,635 --> 00:47:21,126
What are you gonna do with your $20,000?

769
00:47:21,205 --> 00:47:24,038
Buy a giraffe.
What are you gonna do with your $20,000?

770
00:47:24,107 --> 00:47:25,574
Quit school.

771
00:47:25,642 --> 00:47:29,806
Good idea, school is for fools. Look at me!

772
00:47:55,239 --> 00:47:57,139
The park is beautiful.

773
00:47:58,041 --> 00:48:01,636
These trees, they remind you
of Winchestertonfieldville at all?

774
00:48:02,746 --> 00:48:05,078
Oh, yes. Very much so.

775
00:48:05,749 --> 00:48:07,876
What was it like growing up there?

776
00:48:08,018 --> 00:48:09,144
It was great.

777
00:48:09,987 --> 00:48:13,753
I remember walking down
to the corner drugstore...

778
00:48:13,824 --> 00:48:16,122
...and getting malted milkshakes.

779
00:48:17,227 --> 00:48:19,024
What was your house like?

780
00:48:19,496 --> 00:48:21,794
We had this big Victorian.

781
00:48:22,499 --> 00:48:24,194
Right off Main Street.

782
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:29,168
-Blue shutters and a big red door.
-All right.

783
00:48:29,706 --> 00:48:33,642
-And a tire swing in the front yard.
-I love it.

784
00:48:34,077 --> 00:48:38,639
And I remember the time I fell out of
old Boo Radley's apple tree...

785
00:48:38,749 --> 00:48:40,114
...and broke my arm.

786
00:48:40,817 --> 00:48:45,220
And my father, before he passed away...

787
00:48:45,656 --> 00:48:47,920
...from the disease of the lepers...

788
