-No, it was a long time ago.

804
00:49:44,414 --> 00:49:46,177
But my grandma said to me:

805
00:49:46,550 --> 00:49:49,781
"One day you'll grow up
and work for 60 Minutes...

806
00:49:49,853 --> 00:49:51,946
"...and make a difference in the world."

807
00:49:52,856 --> 00:49:56,417
You do make a difference in the world,
every day. You're a school nurse.

808
00:50:00,063 --> 00:50:02,224
Anyways, this is what happened to my uncle.

809
00:50:02,299 --> 00:50:06,497
Later on in his life, he'd go
to this radio station that he owned...

810
00:50:06,570 --> 00:50:09,505
...at 3:00 in the morning and DJ for an hour.

811
00:50:09,573 --> 00:50:10,835
That's great.

812
00:50:11,842 --> 00:50:15,005
So, don't give up hope.
You'll be a reporter someday.

813
00:50:15,579 --> 00:50:17,171
If you really want to.

814
00:50:18,648 --> 00:50:20,240
That would be nice.

815
00:50:23,353 --> 00:50:25,480
-Jeesum Crow, a fire!
-A fire?

816
00:50:25,989 --> 00:50:27,854
-We should help.
-We should?

817
00:50:27,924 --> 00:50:29,858
-Let's get going.
-To the fire?

818
00:50:30,494 --> 00:50:34,157
-Fifi, get over here right now.
-Come on, we'll catch you.

819
00:50:34,498 --> 00:50:37,729
Go away! I can't leave without my kitties.
They're all I got.

820
00:50:39,102 --> 00:50:40,000
Crazy lady!

821
00:50:40,070 --> 00:50:43,096
-Oh, babies, where are you?
